{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Jupyter Notebooks Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Pick your interface"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Three options, one format:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Interface | Install | Best for |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "|-----------|---------|----------|"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| JupyterLab | `pip install jupyterlab` then `jupyter lab` | Full IDE experience, multiple tabs, file browser, terminal |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Jupyter Notebook | `pip install notebook` then `jupyter notebook` | Simple, lightweight, one notebook at a time |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| VS Code | Install \"Jupyter\" extension | Already in your editor, git integration, debugging |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "All three read and write the same `.ipynb` file. Pick whatever you like. JupyterLab is the most common in AI work."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "pip install jupyterlab"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "jupyter lab"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Keyboard shortcuts that matter"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "You operate in two modes. Press `Escape` for command mode (blue bar on the left), `Enter` for edit mode (green bar)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Command mode (most used):**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Key | Action |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "|-----|--------|"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `Shift+Enter` | Run cell, move to next |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `A` | Insert cell above |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `B` | Insert cell below |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `DD` | Delete cell |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `M` | Convert to markdown |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `Y` | Convert to code |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `Z` | Undo cell operation |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `Ctrl+Shift+H` | Show all shortcuts |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Edit mode:**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Key | Action |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "|-----|--------|"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `Tab` | Autocomplete |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `Shift+Tab` | Show function signature |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| `Ctrl+/` | Toggle comment |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`Shift+Enter` is the one you'll use a thousand times a day. Learn it first."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Cell types"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Code cells** run Python and show the output:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "data = np.random.randn(1000)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "data.mean(), data.std()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Output: `(0.0032, 0.9987)`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Markdown cells** render formatted text. Use them to document what you're doing and why. Supports headers, bold, italic, LaTeX math (`$E = mc^2$`), tables, and images."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Magic commands"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "These aren't Python. They're Jupyter-specific commands that start with `%` (line magic) or `%%` (cell magic)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Time your code:**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "%timeit np.random.randn(10000)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Output: `45.2 us +/- 1.3 us per loop`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "%%time"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model.fit(X_train, y_train, epochs=10)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Output: `Wall time: 2.34 s`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`%timeit` runs the code many times and averages. `%%time` runs it once. Use `%timeit` for microbenchmarks, `%%time` for training runs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Enable inline plots:**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "%matplotlib inline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Every `plt.plot()` or `plt.show()` now renders directly in the notebook."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Install packages without leaving the notebook:**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "!pip install scikit-learn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The `!` prefix runs any shell command."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Check environment variables:**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "%env CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Display rich output inline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Notebooks auto-display the last expression in a cell. But you can control it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "df = pd.DataFrame({"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"model\": [\"Linear\", \"Random Forest\", \"Neural Net\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"accuracy\": [0.72, 0.89, 0.94],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"training_time\": [0.1, 2.3, 45.6]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "})"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "df"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "This renders a formatted HTML table, not a text dump. Same with plots:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 4))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "plt.plot([1, 2, 3, 4], [1, 4, 2, 3])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "plt.title(\"Inline Plot\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The plot appears right below the cell. This is why notebooks dominate AI work. You see the data, the plot, and the code together."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For images:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from IPython.display import Image, display"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "display(Image(filename=\"architecture.png\"))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: Google Colab"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Colab is a free Jupyter notebook in the cloud. It gives you a GPU, pre-installed libraries, and Google Drive integration. No setup required."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "1. Go to [colab.research.google.com](https://colab.research.google.com)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "2. Upload any `.ipynb` file from this course"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "3. Runtime > Change runtime type > T4 GPU (free)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Colab differences from local Jupyter:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Files don't persist between sessions (save to Drive or download)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Pre-installed: numpy, pandas, matplotlib, torch, tensorflow, sklearn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `from google.colab import files` to upload/download files"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `from google.colab import drive; drive.mount('/content/drive')` for persistent storage"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Sessions time out after 90 minutes of inactivity (free tier)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Open JupyterLab, create a notebook, and use `%timeit` to compare list comprehension vs numpy for creating an array of 100,000 random numbers\n2. Create a notebook with both markdown and code cells that loads a CSV, displays a dataframe, and plots a chart. Then run Kernel > Restart & Run All to verify it works top to bottom\n3. Take the code from `code/notebook_tips.py`, paste it into a Colab notebook, and run it with a free GPU"
      ]
    }
  ],
